  {
    "sha": "9b79a44b61a1a6e06991af2dfe0c6db2ec846a98",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDliNzlhNDRiNjFhMWE2ZTA2OTkxYWYyZGZlMGM2ZGIyZWM4NDZhOTg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T23:32:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T23:32:54Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(2d): trochoidal method for 2D Adaptive, confined to its region\n\n2D Adaptive gains a Method: Spiral (the default - the HSM plan the kind\nalways ran, byte for byte, same stamp) or Trochoidal. The trochoidal\nmethod cuts one lane of trochoid loops along the medial line of the\ncutter-centre area (the region eroded by the tool radius and the stock\nto leave), its loop band the least clearance along that line, planned by\nthe Trochoidal slot's measured-engagement ladder. The finished path is\nthen checked move by move against the area; a point outside refuses the\noperation by name. A band wider than the tool gets an opened bore (a\nhelix at half the tool radius, then a two-centre semicircle spiral out\nto the band) so no post is left at the lane's start.\n\nRefused by name: a region narrower than the tool, too narrow to loop in,\na ring round an island, a region with no single medial line, a lane that\nwould leave more than 25 % of the region out of reach, a loop outside\nthe region, a drop past the helix turn cap, the Adaptive doors.\n\nThe method is an EditOperationParams edit, the `method` word of\n`adaptive2_d` in the project file (absent reads as spiral) and so an MCP\n`edit_operation` parameter, and a combo on the Passes tab.\n\nRefs #1509\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
